# Inactive historical capture preparation

`capture.produce(fresh_owned_output, proof_inputs)` reads the exact physical .11 input set and writes unsigned capture proposals. It does not activate a catalogue, change a seal or install a lock.
The finite input set contains 66 roles: 52 exact raw aliases and fourteen bounded gzip captures. Captured programs remain passive evidence. Actual program sources and selected proof origins are recorded and rechecked before writing.
Every input, member, aggregate phase and input/output framing bound remains enforced. Fresh output is restricted to the configured Samsung build root; existing output is preserved.
The shared fixture bootstrap whole-pins actual D/G/C/capture sources, normalizes only the single reviewed future policy/catalogue seal and executes the original actual source bytes.
The historical fixture reader admits the exact .11 baseline or the fixed verified historical catalogue behind .12. It rejects unknown versions and missing or changed evidence.
All 19 derive/guard and 24 constructor cases remain. New capture tests use staged physical inputs and do not establish actual catalogue, generator or .12 adoption acceptance.
Actual generator source, strict legacy facade, manually reviewed seals, real default normative/generator/snapshot checks, native/UI/backend restart and full SysON parity remain separate required gates.
